text:
{
  "errors": [
    {
      "span": "If it be said that Breath cannot be Vishnu, as the speaker declares himself to be breath,",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "the objection is to be rejected as not valid,",
      "category": "addition",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "for in this context, the references to the Lord's presence in the many embodied things are numerous.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "According to the text\n\"Breath indeed am I, O sage\" (A. A. ii. 2.3)",
      "category": "terminology",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "the speaker declaring himself to be breath it may be stated that Indra the speaker should be taken to be breath.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "But this view cannot be taken ;",
      "category": "addition",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "\" Breath thou art, Breath are all the beings,\"",
      "category": "fluency",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "and thus points to the relation with (pervasion of) the Lord in the plurality of bodies (things) for,",
      "category": "omission",
      "severity": "major"
    }
  ]
}
